# Criteria recorded before reading std-2.md

Authority: docs/spec.md first; syntax.md; accepted std-1.md contracts and compiler prerequisite; scoped literal-types/records/value-types/types-joint rules; runtime/host-concurrency IO boundary. The task's standalone/no-special-library-rule principles apply throughout.

1. All APIs must be ordinary nominal types, functions, errors, and call-time services; signatures must be rank-one, principal, and preserve service-argument equality. No keyword, runner registration, reflective derivation, special library inference or automatic sink is permitted. Hidden construction invariants must actually be enforced. Prefer few independent operations with laws; judge imported ideas by fit, not familiarity.
2. Duration is exact signed arithmetic; distinguish wall instants from monotonic readings and calendar periods. Int has no overflow (spec 11.2). Specify units, epoch, subtraction orientation, division by zero, negative quotient/remainder, rounding ties, serialization round trips and any bounded wire conversions. Test -1 ns, -1.5 s, positive/negative divisors, enormous values beyond 64 bits.
3. Calendar must specify astronomical year numbering/year zero, proleptic Gregorian leaps including negative centuries, weekday origin, civil/day bijection, offset sign/range, date/time validation, no leap seconds, month-end policy, and distinction of elapsed time vs months. Test -400/-100/-1/0/1/1900/2000, epoch -1 ns, cross-midnight offsets, 9999/10000, huge positive/negative years, month shifting Jan 31/Feb 29, parse/format asymmetry and fixed-offset normalization.
4. CLI descriptions must determine token consumption independently of parser composition. Test duplicate long/short definitions; shared references; repeated flags/options; attached equals and empty values; short clusters; -1 and -; missing values before -- or another option; options after positionals; -- marker; leftovers; optional/repeated positionals; subcommands; help mixed with errors; parser callback ordering; deterministic help and diagnostics; no reflection over application record fields.
5. Logging must preserve sink errors/environment through generic helpers and wrapper constructors. Test pure sink, failing sink, service-using sink, generic forwarding, two unrelated effect instances, replacement at call time, filtered callback evaluation, duplicate structured fields, sink failure/recursion and service argument variance. Isolate E0505 without log types to distinguish a compiler defect from forbidden higher-rank or recursive types. Closed specializations alone do not prove a generic contract.
6. Pure modules should compile/test without IO and future adapters should fit existing representations without dependency cycles. Verify each cited implementation location, reserve IO operations explicitly, and do not call a required compiler conformance fix a new library-specific feature.

Findings require a concrete contradictory outcome, unsupported necessary implementation step, or higher-source conflict. Missing optional API breadth or stylistic preferences alone are not findings. For each decision identify supporting source/reason, falsifying evidence, and simpler alternative.
